{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/810347-what-kind-of-games-to-kindred-play","id":810347,"title":"What kind of games to Kindred play ?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-16T14:02:20-08:00","id":810347,"title":"What kind of games to Kindred play ?","content":"I've herd about Kindred enjoying different games. I was hoping someone could give me an idea for some of these games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T17:58:14-08:00","id":810422,"title":"","content":"Well, many Kindred would enjoy the same sort of mortal games they liked during their lifetime. This means that for some older kindred their requiems may include things which have gone out of fashion and many may have difficulty adapting to the new technological games of the more recent generations. They would have some new difficulties keeping their old hobbies active, particularly for activities that would be done during the day.<br /> <br /> As for new games that only kindred play? Well, I imagine that competitive hunting (of humans mostly) would probably be a sport many of them could enjoy. The Gangrel may enjoy extreme sports type things that get them out into the wild. Mountain-climbing without ropes, hiking through extreme environments with the additional challenge of remaining safe through the day. For the most part I imagine they would just be extreme versions of human hobbies, made possible through their enhanced abilities. The Kindred are often challenged at creating true originality. <br /> <br /> Even the immortal kindred though, still don't have enough time in their requiems to play Monopoly. No one has that sort of time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T19:10:33-08:00","id":810446,"title":"","content":"I picture a lot of Elders favoring abstract strategy like chess, go, mancala, and the like. Some particularly ancient vampires might play historical variants of tables games like backgammon. Younger vampires I could see playing modern board games like Catan. I've always been entertained by the thought of playing D&amp;D as characters in a CofD game, but it'd probably be too meta to really work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T03:02:08-08:00","id":810557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Kenner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/810347-what-kind-of-games-to-kindred-play?p=810422#post810422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even the immortal kindred though, still don't have enough time in their requiems to play Monopoly. No one has that sort of time.</div> </div> </div> </div>The risk of Frenzy is too great as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T04:33:39-08:00","id":810570,"title":"","content":"They actually covered some of these games in the Invictus book. Some of the challenges involved scavanger hunts - as in, you have to hunt someone with a red sport's car, and get a selfie of you in that car with the prey. Or a blonde woman in a grocery store holding a watermelon. Hoax is another game - create false news stories and try to have them published in official news outlets, have it stand up to scrutiny; the more outragous that succeeds, the better. Another was a capture-people-hunt-in-wilderness type equestrian hunt, like old school fox hunting with nobles. Duels and competition are pretty common, both gladitorial and artistic/musical. Modified sports are common in a lot of cities - detroit is especially notorious for it. Board games are pretty common as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 01-17-2016, 07:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T06:05:43-08:00","id":810593,"title":"","content":"How does one avoid Frenzy when smack talk goes flying around? More importantly, how are duels even possible when you start rolling Frenzy checks at first injury? It seems like a potential fun-ruiner for Kindred games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T13:22:19-08:00","id":810779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/810347-what-kind-of-games-to-kindred-play?p=810593#post810593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does one avoid Frenzy when smack talk goes flying around? More importantly, how are duels even possible when you start rolling Frenzy checks at first injury? It seems like a potential fun-ruiner for Kindred games.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Easy, if you frenzy then you automatically lose the game/duel and suffer great shame. The Invictus is built upon status and honor so no self respecting vampire would enter a game without being confident that they had the personal resolve to resist frenzy.<br /> <br /> Also, this means that duels, rather than being death matches, are instead contests to force your opponent to frenzy or in some other way be disqualified. The purpose of duels is to settle conflicts without resorting to murder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8306,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8306-wissenschaft","user":"Wissenschaft","date":". 01-17-2016, 04:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8306-wissenschaft","name":"Wissenschaft","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T19:24:55-08:00","id":810915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wissenschaft</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/810347-what-kind-of-games-to-kindred-play?p=810779#post810779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Easy, if you frenzy then you automatically lose the game/duel and suffer great shame. The Invictus is built upon status and honor so no self respecting vampire would enter a game without being confident that they had the personal resolve to resist frenzy.<br /> <br /> Also, this means that duels, rather than being death matches, are instead contests to force your opponent to frenzy or in some other way be disqualified. The purpose of duels is to settle conflicts without resorting to murder.</div> </div> </div> </div>In this context, the Taunt maneuver in the Kindred Dueling style becomes <i>very</i> appealing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T19:39:08-08:00","id":810922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/810347-what-kind-of-games-to-kindred-play?p=810915#post810915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In this context, the Taunt maneuver in the Kindred Dueling style becomes <i>very</i> appealing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yup. I find the Invictus sourcebook a wonderful treasure trove of info on how &quot;polite&quot; undead society operates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8306-wissenschaft","name":"Wissenschaft","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T06:25:06-08:00","id":811082,"title":"","content":"Invictus Book is indeed wonderful. Other games I've seen played among Kindred players that I thought were clever (1e and 2e):<br /> <br /> <i>Amazing Race</i> - Protean users pick different forms (Land, Sea, and Air) or (Fight and Flight) and put them through the paces.<br /> <br /> <i>Truth and Consequences</i> - Two or more kindred with Telepathy link their minds. They take turns digging into each others thoughts for secrets or shames to write down. The contestant that the secret is about has a chance to see what is written and forfeit so that the secret isn't revealed. Otherwise, it's read to the audience who later determine which contestant revealed the more intense / embarrassing / surprising tidbits.<br /> <br /> <i>Breakdown</i> - Contestants take turns sculpting an unaware kindred's requiem events and surroundings such that they are placed in situations where they are tempted to violate their self-declared morals (humanity checks). Contestants are not allowed to influence the victim directly, but can influence friends / family / co-workers / touchstones / allies, etc. The more subtle the changes when forcing the moral break, the more 'points' are scored. A version called <i>hot-potato</i> involves taking a victim as close to humanity zero as possible, with the contestant who actually tips the victim into a permanent frenzy declared the loser.<br /> <br /> <i>Spiritcraft</i> - Contestants are each given items with no spiritual resonance. They orchestrate events around the item such that impressions are left and readable through Spirit's Touch. To offset pure violence (often the easiest way to leave intense impressions) - emotional themes can be introduced (Impressions of love, despair, want, indifference, etc.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T07:24:34-08:00","id":811099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/810347-what-kind-of-games-to-kindred-play?p=810446#post810446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I picture a lot of Elders favoring abstract strategy like chess, go, mancala, and the like. Some particularly ancient vampires might play historical variants of tables games like backgammon. Younger vampires I could see playing modern board games like Catan. I've always been entertained by the thought of playing D&amp;D as characters in a CofD game, but it'd probably be too meta to really work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Off-Topic, but one of my players did that in Mage. A D&amp;D nerd who became a wizard for real.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T12:25:36-08:00","id":811257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/810347-what-kind-of-games-to-kindred-play?p=810446#post810446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I picture a lot of Elders favoring abstract strategy like chess, go, mancala, and the like. Some particularly ancient vampires might play historical variants of tables games like backgammon. Younger vampires I could see playing modern board games like Catan. I've always been entertained by the thought of playing D&amp;D as characters in a CofD game, but it'd probably be too meta to really work.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd personally go for Mage: the Ascension. They want to pretend to be able to turn their elders to lawn chairs and improve their condition. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> To answer the question, for board and card games it will depend on their age, if you want to be in your elder's good books it's time to start learning chess, go, backgammon, and other older games. I can see various types of poker being played, of course using mortal pawns as wagers, with tables ranked according to political power (that actually gives me an idea for an interesting Elyssium), where EVERYBODY is trying to get away with using Auspex and/or Majesty. For younger kindred look towards more modern games, I can see a version of Agricola that exchanges farms for feeding grounds, and a game of Dominion among Neonates could be interesting. Don't get me started on the local Kindred Diplomacy club, they can't even manage to divide into groups to play anymore. So basically what Charlaquin said.<br /> <br /> For more physical games and/or sports? I have no idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T12:58:01-08:00","id":811273,"title":"","content":"Of course, kindred now adapt much more quickly to innovation after emerging from Torpor; so yeah, I'm absolutely going to have social competitions and chess, and enjoy the hell out of it, but I <i>personally </i>am going to have a lot more fun with the Prince who spends his time between appointments furiously pushing an Angry Birds high score, or the Elysium socialite who gets blackmailed because he's found that camping and screaming at f*****s on Call Of Duty: The Et Cetera Missions sates his Beast in a way he never anticipated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}